# Everything the smoke image installs, and nothing else.
#
# The list is short on purpose. This image exists to find out whether a
# Hyprland session comes up on ZepOS's generated configuration; every
# package that is not needed to answer that is one more thing that can
# fail for a reason nobody is interested in. A workstation needs roughly
# a hundred and forty packages - that is zepos-desktop and the shipping
# image of TP5-2, not this.
#
# Deliberately absent:
#   linux-firmware  - a virtio guest needs no device firmware, and it is
#                     the single largest package in the image.

# --- ZepOS's own, out of the [zepos] repository -----------------------
# These lines are what replaced iso/build.sh copying src/ into the image
# by hand. The difference is not cosmetic: a copy tests a layout that
# never ships, and it can only ever carry files - a package carries
# dependencies, file modes, an /etc/skel default and a signature, and
# every one of those is a thing that can be wrong somewhere a copy
# cannot be wrong at all.
#
# zepos-config puts the templates, the styles and the generator in
# /usr/share/zepos and the three commands in /usr/bin.
#
# aylurs-gtk-shell is the reason the first boot of this image could not
# show a single AGS widget: AGS is in no Arch repository (spec §4.3), so
# the fifteen AGS templates generated files with nothing to run them. It
# pulls libastal-io and libastal-4 in with it.
#
# libastal-notifd is named here although AGS only suggests it, because
# ags-notifications.template imports AstalNotifd on its fifth line and
# app.ts imports that widget at the top level: without the typelib the
# WHOLE bundle fails at import time and no widget starts, not just the
# notifications.
zepos-config
aylurs-gtk-shell
libastal-notifd

# zepos-keyring is here for the one thing a container cannot supply: it
# is the only ZepOS package with an install scriptlet, and the
# conditions that scriptlet was written for exist during a real
# pacstrap and nowhere else. mkarchiso passes -G, so the image being
# built has no pacman keyring in it at all; the scriptlet has to notice
# that and skip rather than fail, or this build stops.
# packaging/verify-install.sh measures the other half, where a keyring
# does exist and the population actually happens.
#
# It also puts the key material on the live medium, which is what
# `pacman-key --init && pacman-key --populate zepos` in a live session
# needs before anything can be installed from [zepos] (spec §8.4).
zepos-keyring

# --- the installer, which is what makes this a ZepOS ISO --------------
# Spec §4.2, one line under the table: "Die drei Installer-Pakete liegen
# nur in der ISO, nicht im installierten System." Both halves of that
# sentence are now measured. This is the first half; the second is
# packaging/verify-install.sh's third container, which installs
# zepos-desktop and checks that zepos-installer, -gui, -tui and
# archinstall are all absent afterwards.
#
# All three, not only the core: §8.5's fallback from GTK4 to the text
# interface is a decision taken at run time on the machine in front of
# the user, so both surfaces have to be present for it to be a decision
# rather than a foregone conclusion. zepos-installer-gui is the only one
# of the three that names a toolkit.
#
# zepos-installer brings archinstall with it, which is what actually
# partitions, bootstraps and installs a bootloader - spec §8.1: "Ein
# eigener Partitionierer waere Code, dessen Fehler fremde Festplatten
# loeschen." It also brings util-linux, openssl and iwd, one for each
# thing installer/core calls directly: lsblk for the disk list, `openssl
# passwd -6` for the password hashes, iwctl for the wireless step.
#
# This is what the image had never carried, and it is why "ZepOS has
# never been installed" was still true after three boots of it.
zepos-installer
zepos-installer-gui
zepos-installer-tui

# The five plugins of spec §7.1, which is what makes plugins.conf a file
# with load lines in it rather than eighty-one lines of comment
# explaining what is missing. src/plugins.py keeps a plugin's block only
# when /usr/lib/hyprland/plugins/<name>.so is on the machine at the
# moment the file is generated, so their presence in the IMAGE is what
# the smoke run measures - and their absence would look exactly like a
# working desktop with no title bars, no zones and a launcher that
# fell back to zepos-menu.
zepos-hyprbars
zepos-borders-plus-plus
zepos-hyprlaunch
zepos-hyprclipx
zepos-hyprzones

# `ags run` compiles the style.scss that ags-style.template generates by
# shelling out to dart-sass. Without it the bundle has no stylesheet.
dart-sass

# --- archiso baseline: without these the image does not boot ---------
base
linux
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
syslinux

# --- the compositor, and what a machine without a GPU needs to draw ---
# mesa carries the software rasteriser. QEMU's virtio-gpu offers a KMS
# device with dumb buffers and no render node, so Mesa's kms_swrast is
# the only path from Hyprland's GBM/EGL requirement to a framebuffer.
#
# zepos-hyprland and not hyprland: spec §4.2 and §7. Hyprland stood in
# §4.3's list of packages usable straight out of extra until the revision
# to §7 took it back out, because five plugin packages are compiled
# against its headers and cannot have their compositor move underneath
# them on somebody else's release schedule. It provides `hyprland` and
# conflicts with it, so xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland below resolves
# against it and the two can never both be installed.
zepos-hyprland
mesa
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
polkit
polkit-gnome

# --- what the generated hyprland.conf actually starts -----------------
# waybar und nwg-dock-hyprland standen hier und sind am 11.08.2026
# entfallen: beide sind GTK3 (waybar auf gtkmm-3, nwg-dock ohne jede
# GTK4-Fassung), und Leiste wie Dock sind seither Fenster in AGS -
# ags/widget/Bar.tsx und ags/widget/Dock.tsx, GTK4 ueber libastal-4.
kitty
zepos-menu
wl-clipboard
cliphist
swaybg
xsettingsd
numlockx
brightnessctl

# DIE ABMELDEMASKE STEHT NICHT MEHR ALS EIGENES PAKET HIER
#     Bis zum 19.08.2026 (Aufgabe 26) stand hier `zepos-logout`, ein
#     eigenes gebautes Paket - hyprland-universal-config.template band
#     SUPER+M unbedingt darauf, und ohne die Zeile waere die Taste auf
#     dem Medium tot gewesen. Davor, bis zum 11.08.2026, stand hier
#     `wlogout`, verworfen aus demselben Grund, den logout/zepos-logout.c
#     einmal fuehrte: gemessen auf libgtk-3.so.0, waehrend die
#     Entscheidung vom 11.08.2026 die Oberflaeche durchgehend auf GTK4
#     stellt.
#
#     zepos-logout selbst ist mit Aufgabe 26 geloescht (Regel 14): das
#     Programm ist einem AGS-Fenster gewichen
#     (src/templates/ags-logout.template), SUPER+M ruft seither
#     `ags request logout`. `aylurs-gtk-shell` weiter oben in dieser
#     Datei installiert dieses Fenster bereits mit - es gibt kein
#     zweites Paket mehr, das hier zusaetzlich stehen muesste.

# DER SPERRBILDSCHIRM STEHT ABSICHTLICH NICHT HIER
#     zepos-lock gibt es seit dem 12.08.2026, hyprland-universal-config.
#     template bindet SUPER+L unbedingt darauf, und trotzdem gehoert es
#     nicht in dieses Bild. Der Grund ist gemessen und steht zwei Dateien
#     weiter:
#
#         airootfs/etc/sysusers.d/zepos.conf
#           u zepos 1000 "ZepOS live session" /home/zepos /bin/bash
#
#     systemd-sysusers legt ein Konto mit GESPERRTEM Passwortfeld an -
#     airootfs/etc/systemd/system/getty@tty1.service.d/autologin.conf
#     sagt es selbst ("The account systemd-sysusers creates has a locked
#     password field"), und deshalb funktioniert die Anmeldung dort nur
#     ueber `agetty --autologin`.
#
#     pam_unix kann gegen ein gesperrtes Feld nicht abgleichen, und
#     `nullok` hilft dabei nicht: das erlaubt ein LEERES Feld, nicht ein
#     gesperrtes. Ein Sperrbildschirm auf dem Medium wiese also JEDES
#     Passwort ab - und weil ext-session-lock-v1 die Sitzung auch beim
#     Absturz des Sperrprogramms gesperrt LAESST, waere der Nutzer bis
#     zum harten Neustart aus dem Installationsassistenten ausgesperrt.
#
#     SUPER+L ist auf dem Medium damit eine tote Taste, und das ist die
#     billigere der beiden Moeglichkeiten. Sie war es vorher auch:
#     hyprlock stand hier ebenso wenig. Neu ist nur, dass es jetzt eine
#     Entscheidung ist statt eines Versehens -
#     tests/iso/test_smoke_profile.py haelt sie fest.

# --- grim is evidence, not decoration --------------------------------
# It captures what the compositor rendered, from inside the session.
# QEMU's framebuffer dump proves the screen shows something; grim proves
# the something came out of Hyprland.
grim

# --- interpreters the generator and the generated helpers need --------
bash
python
zsh
jq

# --- fonts, or the bar is a row of replacement boxes ------------------
# The whole point of the icon SSOT is Nerd Font glyphs; without the font
# a screenshot cannot distinguish "the bar is there" from "the bar is
# broken".
#
# ZeptronIT's two families are here for the same reason and it is
# stronger, because their absence does NOT look broken: fontconfig
# answers a missing family by substituting one it has, so a screenshot of
# a machine without them shows a working desktop in the wrong typeface -
# which is exactly what this image exists to be unable to say.
# zepos-desktop depends on both; the image installs them directly
# because it does not install zepos-desktop.
ttf-fira-code
ttf-roboto
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd
ttf-dejavu
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji

# --- GTK stack and icons for the widgets that do exist ----------------
gtk3
gtk4
papirus-icon-theme
adwaita-icon-theme

# --- named by the generated status scripts ----------------------------
networkmanager
